sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To describe a rectilinear figure similar and similarly situated to a given rectilinear figure on a given straight line.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be the given straight line and {CE|CEt} the given rectilinear figure.

It is required to describe on the straight line {AB} a rectilinear figure similar and similarly situated to the rectilinear figure {CE|CEt}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="350" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.18 diagram" src="propVI18.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure draws the given quadrilateral CDEF, the join DF, and
    // the triangles ABG (similar to CDF) and BGH (similar to DFE), all with
    // random faces; G and H are derived (similar).
    //
    // The walk builds the new figure line by line, so AB, AG, BG, GH, BH
    // are solid slide twins over the triangles' edges, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden), stroking from A, B, G, B as constructed; the
    // filled triangles come back on the closing slide. DF is Joyce's own
    // line, declared D to F, and is simply withheld until "Join DF".
    // Everything else added is transparent: the sides FC, CD, FE, ED, and
    // faceless polygons for "the rectilinear figures" CE (CEt) and AH (AHt)
    // and the four triangles FCD, GAB, FDE, GBH (a highlighted filled
    // polygon is raised over the figure, #140). Equal angles share a
    // colour; none is a right angle. The triangles own the names GAB, FDE,
    // GBH, ABG, BGH; the angles take display overrides.
    var GIVEN = ["CDEF","C","D","E","F","AB","A","B"];
    var JOIN  = GIVEN.concat(["DF"]);
    var TRI1  = JOIN.concat(["AG","BG","G"]);
    var TRI2  = TRI1.concat(["GH","BH","H"]);
    var SIDES = ["FC","CD","FE","ED"];
    var ANG1  = ["angC","angA","angCDF","angABG","angCFD","angAGB"];
    var ANG2  = ["angDFE","angBGH","angFDE","angGBH","angE","angH"];
    var WHOLE = ["angCFE","angAGH","angCDE","angABH"];
    var ALL   = TRI2.concat(SIDES, ANG1, ANG2);
    var DONE  = TRI2.concat(["ABG","BGH"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.18",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,240;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,240;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,220,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,310,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,160,0",
            "E;point;free;130,30",
            "F;point;free;60,130",
            "CDEF;polygon;quadrilateral;C,D,E,F;0;0;black;random",
            "DF;line;connect;D,F",
            "G;point;similar;A,B,C,D,F",
            "ABG;polygon;triangle;A,B,G;0;0;black;random",
            "H;point;similar;B,G,D,F,E",
            "BGH;polygon;triangle;B,G,H;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide twins, hidden at rest (see above).
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G",
            "BG;line;connect;B,G",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H",
            "BH;line;connect;B,H",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "FC;line;connect;F,C;0;0;0",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D;0;0;0",
            "FE;line;connect;F,E;0;0;0",
            "ED;line;connect;E,D;0;0;0",
            "CEt;polygon;quadrilateral;C,D,E,F;0;0;0;0",
            "AHt;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,H,G;0;0;0;0",
            "FCD;polygon;triangle;F,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            "GAB;polygon;triangle;G,A,B;0;0;0;0",
            "FDE;polygon;triangle;F,D,E;0;0;0;0",
            "GBH;polygon;triangle;G,B,H;0;0;0;0",
            // Angle markers; equal angles share a colour.
            "angC;sector;angleMarker;C,D,F;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angA;sector;angleMarker;A,B,G;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angCDF;sector;angleMarker;D,C,F;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angABG;sector;angleMarker;B,A,G;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angCFD;sector;angleMarker;F,C,D;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angAGB;sector;angleMarker;G,A,B;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angDFE;sector;angleMarker;F,D,E;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angBGH;sector;angleMarker;G,B,H;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angFDE;sector;angleMarker;D,F,E;0;0;b5446e;f0b6cb",
            "angGBH;sector;angleMarker;B,G,H;0;0;b5446e;f0b6cb",
            "angE;sector;angleMarker;E,D,F;0;0;2a8a8a;a6dede",
            "angH;sector;angleMarker;H,B,G;0;0;2a8a8a;a6dede",
            "angCFE;sector;angleMarker;F,C,E;0;0;8a6d3b;e0cfa8",
            "angAGH;sector;angleMarker;G,A,H;0;0;8a6d3b;e0cfa8",
            "angCDE;sector;angleMarker;D,C,E;0;0;5a5a5a;c8c8c8",
            "angABH;sector;angleMarker;B,A,H;0;0;5a5a5a;c8c8c8"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): the track ends A0, A3
        // (free, off-canvas), the lineSliders A, B, C, D and the free E, F —
        // all givens, standing from slide 1; nothing to defer. G and H are
        // derived and listed per slide.
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","AG","BG","GH","BH"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "GA": "AG", "GB": "BG", "HG": "GH",
                   "HB": "BH", "FD": "DF", "CF": "FC", "DC": "CD",
                   "EF": "FE", "DE": "ED", "CE": "CEt", "AH": "AHt",
                   "CDF": "angCDF", "FDC": "angCDF",
                   "CFD": "angCFD", "DFC": "angCFD",
                   "AGB": "angAGB", "BGA": "angAGB",
                   "DFE": "angDFE", "EFD": "angDFE",
                   "CFE": "angCFE", "EFC": "angCFE",
                   "AGH": "angAGH", "HGA": "angAGH",
                   "CDE": "angCDE", "EDC": "angCDE",
                   "ABH": "angABH", "HBA": "angABH" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To describe a rectilinear figure similar and similarly situated to a given rectilinear figure on a given straight line.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CEt","AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.18" }] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be the given straight line and {CE|CEt} the given rectilinear figure.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CEt"] },
            { text: "It is required to describe on the straight line {AB} a rectilinear figure",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "similar and similarly situated to the rectilinear figure {CE|CEt}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["CEt"] },
            { text: "Join {DF}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["DF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Construct the angle {GAB|angA} equal to the angle at {C|angC},",
              visible: JOIN.concat(["AG","angC","angA"]),
              highlighted: ["angA","angC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "AG",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle GAB = angle C", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "and the angle {ABG|angABG} equal to the angle {CDF|angCDF},",
              visible: TRI1.concat(["angC","angA","angCDF","angABG"]),
              highlighted: ["angABG","angCDF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCDF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "BG",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angABG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "G",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle ABG = angle CDF", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "on the straight line {AB} at the points {A} and {B} on it.",
              visible: TRI1.concat(["angC","angA","angCDF","angABG"]),
              highlighted: ["AB","A","B"] },
            { text: "Therefore the remaining angle {CFD|angCFD} equals the angle {AGB|angAGB}.",
              visible: TRI1.concat(ANG1),
              highlighted: ["angCFD","angAGB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCFD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angAGB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "remaining angle CFD = AGB", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {FCD} is equiangular with the triangle {GAB}.",
              visible: TRI1.concat(ANG1),
              highlighted: ["FCD","GAB"] },
            { text: "Therefore, proportionally, {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FC} is to {GA|AG}, and as {CD} is to {AB}.",
              visible: TRI1.concat(ANG1, ["FC","CD"]),
              highlighted: ["DF","BG","FC","AG","CD","AB"],
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "FD : FC = GB : GA, FD : DC = GB : BA", ref: "VI.4" },
                  { claim: "alternately", ref: "V.16" } ] },
            { text: "Again, construct the angle {BGH|angBGH} equal to the angle {DFE|angDFE},",
              visible: TRI1.concat(["GH","angDFE","angBGH"]),
              highlighted: ["angBGH","angDFE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angDFE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "GH",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angBGH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle BGH = angle DFE", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "and the angle {GBH|angGBH} equal to the angle {FDE|angFDE},",
              visible: TRI2.concat(["angDFE","angBGH","angFDE","angGBH"]),
              highlighted: ["angGBH","angFDE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angFDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "BH",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angGBH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "H",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle GBH = angle FDE", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "on the straight line {BG} and at the points {B} and {G} on it.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(["angDFE","angBGH","angFDE","angGBH"]),
              highlighted: ["BG","B","G"] },
            { text: "Therefore the remaining angle at {E|angE} equals the remaining angle at {H|angH}.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(ANG2),
              highlighted: ["angE","angH"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "remaining angle E = H", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {FDE} is equiangular with the triangle {GBH}.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(ANG2),
              highlighted: ["FDE","GBH"] },
            { text: "Therefore, proportionally, {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FE} is to {GH}, and as {ED} is to {HB|BH}.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(ANG2, ["FE","ED"]),
              highlighted: ["DF","BG","FE","GH","ED","BH"],
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "FD : FE = GB : GH, FD : DE = GB : BH", ref: "VI.4" },
                  { claim: "alternately", ref: "V.16" } ] },
            { text: "But it was also proved that {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FC} is to {GA|AG}, and as {CD} is to {AB}.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(SIDES),
              highlighted: ["DF","BG","FC","AG","CD","AB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FC} is to {AG} as {CD} is to {AB},",
              visible: TRI2.concat(SIDES),
              highlighted: ["FC","AG","CD","AB"] },
            { text: "and as {FE} is to {GH}, and further as {ED} is to {HB|BH}.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(SIDES),
              highlighted: ["FC","AG","FE","GH","ED","BH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same with the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "And, since the angle {CFD|angCFD} equals the angle {AGB|angAGB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["angCFD","angAGB"] },
            { text: "and the angle {DFE|angDFE} equals the angle {BGH|angBGH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["angDFE","angBGH"] },
            { text: "therefore the whole angle {CFE|angCFE} equals the whole angle {AGH|angAGH}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(["angCFE","angAGH"]),
              highlighted: ["angCFE","angAGH"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCFE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angAGH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "For the same reason the angle {CDE|angCDE} also equals the angle {ABH|angABH}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: ["angCDE","angABH"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angCDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angABH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "And the angle at {C|angC} also equals the angle at {A|angA},",
              visible: ALL.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: ["angC","angA"] },
            { text: "and the angle at {E|angE} equals the angle at {H|angH}.",
              visible: ALL.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: ["angE","angH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {AH|AHt} is equiangular with {CE|CEt},",
              visible: TRI2.concat(SIDES, ["angC","angA","angE","angH"], WHOLE),
              highlighted: ["AHt","CEt","angC","angA","angE","angH",
                            "angCFE","angAGH","angCDE","angABH"] },
            { text: "and they have the sides about their equal angles proportional.",
              visible: TRI2.concat(SIDES),
              highlighted: ["AB","BH","GH","AG","CD","ED","FE","FC"] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectilinear figure {AH|AHt} is similar to the rectilinear figure {CE|CEt}.",
              visible: TRI2,
              highlighted: ["AHt","CEt"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.Def.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectilinear figure {AH|AHt} has been described similar and similarly situated",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["AHt"] },
            { text: "to the given rectilinear figure {CE|CEt} on the given straight line {AB}.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["CEt","AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.18") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.23":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.32":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "V.11":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "V.16":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV16/",
        "VI.4":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI4/",
        "VI.Def.1": "/elements/books/bookVI/definitions/defVI1/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Join {DF}.  Construct the angle {GAB|angA} equal to the angle at {C|angC}, and the angle {ABG|angABG} equal to the angle {CDF|angCDF}, on the straight line {AB} at the points {A} and {B} on it. [!just I.23]

Therefore the remaining angle {CFD|angCFD} equals the angle {AGB|angAGB}. Therefore the triangle {FCD} is equiangular with the triangle {GAB}. [!just I.32]

Therefore, proportionally, {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FC} is to {GA|AG}, and as {CD} is to {AB}. [!just VI.4; V.16]

Again, construct the angle {BGH|angBGH} equal to the angle {DFE|angDFE}, and the angle {GBH|angGBH} equal to the angle {FDE|angFDE}, on the straight line {BG} and at the points {B} and {G} on it. [!just I.23]

Therefore the remaining angle at {E|angE} equals the remaining angle at {H|angH}.  Therefore the triangle {FDE} is equiangular with the triangle {GBH}.  Therefore, proportionally, {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FE} is to {GH}, and as {ED} is to {HB|BH}. [!just I.32; VI.4; V.16]

But it was also proved that {FD|DF} is to {GB|BG} as {FC} is to {GA|AG}, and as {CD} is to {AB}. Therefore  {FC} is to {AG} as {CD} is to {AB}, and as {FE} is to {GH}, and further as {ED} is to {HB|BH}. [!just V.11]

And, since the angle {CFD|angCFD} equals the angle {AGB|angAGB}, and the angle {DFE|angDFE} equals the angle {BGH|angBGH}, therefore the whole angle {CFE|angCFE} equals the whole angle {AGH|angAGH}.

For the same reason the angle {CDE|angCDE} also equals the angle {ABH|angABH}.

And the angle at {C|angC} also equals the angle at {A|angA}, and the angle at {E|angE} equals the angle at {H|angH}.

Therefore {AH|AHt} is equiangular with {CE|CEt}, and they have the sides about their equal angles proportional.  Therefore the rectilinear figure {AH|AHt} is similar to the rectilinear figure {CE|CEt}. [!just VI.Def.1]

Therefore the rectilinear figure {AH|AHt} has been described similar and similarly situated to the given rectilinear figure {CE|CEt} on the given straight line {AB}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
----
guide:

It is evident from the diagram, if not from the text, that {AB} should correspond to {CD}.

Although the figure has only four sides, it is clear that the method applies to figures with more than four sides.

This proposition is used in the proofs of propositions @VI.22, @VI.25, and @VI.28, and the corollary is used in @XII.17.
